   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "How to use · v1.0.0",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## How to use · v1.0.0\n\n**What it does:** edits one picture from a written instruction with Capybara v0.1 (a Hunyuan Video 1.5 fine-tune), keeping the picture's shape. Core ComfyUI nodes only.\n\n1. **Your inputs** (green group):\n   - **Your picture**: load the picture to edit. It is set to `example.png` (ships with ComfyUI) so the first Run works.\n   - **Edit instruction**: say what to change and what to keep, in English. The text already there (straw hat to red beret) belongs to the README sample photo, not to `example.png`: write your own for your picture.\n   - **Negative prompt**: what to avoid (the template's text).\n   - **Megapixels** (1): size of the result; the picture is resized to this many pixels, shape kept, sides rounded to 16 (1776x1184 in → 1248x832 out at 1.0).\n   - **Steps** (20) and **CFG** (6): the template's values. The authors' code uses 50 steps, CFG 1 and shift 5 for edits (shift is in group 4, node **Shift 7**): tried on both samples, it changed the hat but left the forest half autumn and washed out (44-45 s instead of 39-40 s).\n   - **Seed**: fixed at 24112026. Type a new number for another take; Run with nothing changed does nothing.\n2. **Models**: the four loaders must show the files from the Downloads note. Nothing to change.\n3. **Picture + instruction**: nothing to change; the picture and text come from group 1.\n4. **Sampling**: euler / simple, shift 7. Nothing to change.\n5. Press **Run**. The result is saved by the **Result** node to `output/Capybara/`.\n\n**What to expect:** a 1248x832 edit of a 3:2 picture in about 40 s (20 steps) on the 24 GB lab card, 43-48 s inside a 10-12 GiB VRAM budget. Snow, foliage and other fine detail can carry a fine speckle when you zoom in (see the README).\n\n**Tested on:** ComfyUI 0.45.3, RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell 24 GB, 2026-11-24. Hat edit 40.1 s (first run, models loading), forest edit 39.1 s. In 12 and 10 GiB `--reserve-vram` budgets: 43-48 s, pixel-identical pictures. Not run on a 12 GB card.\n"
   ]
  },
